  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Delhi-Meerut Regional Rapid Transit System Investment Project (Tranche 4)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADB received the periodic financing request for tranche 4 on 19 March 2025. The project is still in line with the Functional Plan on Transport for the NCR, which recommends an integrated multimodal transport system to improve the mobility of people and goods in the NCR. Tranche 4 is aligned with the facility&amp;apos;s impact: urban mobility in the NCR improved. It will have the following outcome: efficiency, safety, social inclusiveness, and environmental sustainability of transport in the Delhi-Meerut RRTS corridor improved. The project is progressing well and all outputs are expected to be completed by 2027. For tranche 4, ADB is reinforcing gender equality and social inclusion (GESI) by including a target for women in institutional capacity development, particularly in project and contract management, financial management, procurement, and safeguards.</narrative>
  </description>
